  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1217 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nWe could see some expanding of a potential Heat Advisory across more \nof the region for Thursday and heat index values will once again \nreach that critical threshold of 108 degrees although ambient \ntemperatures will be slightly lower than that on Wednesday. Right \nnow it will be tough to pinpoint much else in way of temperatures \nfor the rest of the week as we continue to monitor what is now \nTropical Storm Bertha. Bertha became a little more organized between \nnormal advisory times, so a special advisory was issued to name it. \nWhat we do know, Bertha will bring some Tropical Storm conditions to \nportions of the Gulf Coast from Alabama westward to southeastern \nLouisiana. What we don't know, is how this system will impact our \narea. Right now trends are shifting the track a little further to \nthe north, which would be good for limiting the impacts we see here \nin Texas. What you should do, continue to monitor the forecast for \nthe latest information as things could change throughout the next \nfew days. Otherwise, temperatures will remain elevated and near or \nabove normal through the long-term period and mostly dry conditions \n(Tropical Storm Bertha dependent) will remain in place for our \nregion.",
